{"c":[{"id":"8ad2a830a02e02b3","sum":"Model AGENTS.md is on the add-a-model checklist; root README lists no models; don't test Cults User-Agent. CadQuery section(z) follows workplane normal (XZ revolve slices along y). Use true circles, not Shapely polylines; offset touching cones 0.2.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8d80c56c1ac8210e","sum":"Add-a-model checklist includes model AGENTS.md; root README lists no models. Do not test Cults User-Agent (change detector).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261015T154954Z-18a69cbe885816c7","text":"Supersedes the checklist-gap note: the Add-a-model checklist now has the model AGENTS.md step. The root README lists no models on purpose; the directories are the list.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261015T155147Z-711ba3dd8db79ebf","text":"Do not test the Cults User-Agent string. Asserting the header, or that Python-urllib is absent, is a change detector.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"82b21961bd137392","sum":"CadQuery: Workplane.section(z) follows the workplane normal (an XZ revolve slices along y); an area at height z is a thin slab. Shapely polylines bloat STEP and coincident cones are invalid; use true circles and offset touching cones by 0.2.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261015T175712Z-186d790bde4ed5d2","text":"CadQuery: Workplane.section(z) slices along the normal of the workplane the solid came from (a revolve on XZ slices along y). To get an area at height z, intersect a thin slab.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261015T175712Z-8a9b068da52fc102","text":"CadQuery: shapes from shapely polylines bloat STEP (4 MB vs 320 KB) and coincident cones make invalid solids; build from true circles and offset touching cones by 0.2.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"fd8eacd00eaeefe5","sum":"Main only after a photographed print; release publishes to Cults. v6.1: GitHub links OK; free elsewhere stays free; exclusivity is featuring only. Two-model commits hit both changelogs. Match the creation-time slug; version in the description, or blank id opens a second listing.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"31c37213a50ce3af","sum":"Land a model on main only after a verified, photographed test print; a release publishes to Cults. Cults terms v6.1: profile and markdown may link GitHub; Cults may zero a paid price if the file is free elsewhere; selling that is abuse; exclusivity affects featuring only.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261015T180306Z-e51cb22495956e9b","text":"Iterate a model on its own branch; land on main only after a test print is verified and photographed, since a release on main now publishes to Cults.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261015T191113Z-ec972aef108162fe","text":"Cults terms v6.1 (2026-03-31, French controls): profile and markdown descriptions may link GitHub. Cults may zero a paid price if the same file is free elsewhere. Selling a free-elsewhere file is abuse. Exclusivity affects featuring only.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e1ad9944f3840761","sum":"Commit touching two models lands in both changelogs. Cults URL tail is the creation-time title slug; a later title can diverge. Publisher matches the exact name, so a versioned title with a blank cults_creation_id opens a second listing. Keep the version in the description.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261015T191156Z-0211d6cf5f5b64a4","text":"A squash that touches two model directories gives both packages one changelog line: release-please reads only the subject.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261015T191626Z-f508cfadc22886dc","text":"Cults URL last segment is a slug of the title at creation. A later title can diverge from that slug. Publisher matches the exact name, so a versioned title with a blank cults_creation_id opens a second listing. Put the version in the description.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
